---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import EmailSignup from "../components/EmailSignup.astro";
import { DONATION_RAILS } from "../config";
---

<Base title="Transparency" description="What is verified about contributions to The Audacity Network, what Pearl has said they fund, and what still requires confirmation.">
  <span class="pill">What is verified</span>
  <h1>Transparency</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A contribution is a claim on future work. This page separates what the network's
    published terms confirm from Pearl's stated funding priorities. It does not promise
    tax treatment, earmarking, or financial controls that have not been documented.
  </p>

  <h2>The entity that receives donations</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p>
      The Audacity Network's published
      <a href="https://www.theaudacitynetwork.com/terms" rel="noopener">Terms of Service</a>
      identify the operator as <strong>JustPearlyThings, LLC, trading as The Audacity
      Network</strong>, and identify Stripe as the card processor.
    </p>
    <p class="notice" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
      <strong>No tax-deduction claim is made here.</strong> The current support page
      identifies an LLC, not a 501(c)(3). Donors should not treat a contribution as
      tax-deductible unless the checkout identifies a qualified charitable recipient
      and supplies the required receipt.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Pearl's stated funding priorities</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    These priorities come from Pearl's June 2026 public explanation of the network.
    They describe intended use; they are not restricted-fund promises.
  </p>
  <div class="grid cols-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>1. Content production</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Documentaries, daily show, editors, producers, camera and writing. This is the
        priority allocation and it isn't close — no other line item exists if this one
        stops.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>2. Legal defense</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Reporting critically on institutions invites lawsuits, meritorious or not.
        Legal defense is budgeted so the reporting doesn't have to be retracted to
        avoid it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>3. Fieldwork</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Travel and filming — the reporting that requires being physically somewhere,
        with cameras, on someone else's schedule. Receipts are kept and categorized.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>4. Downstream reform (contingent)</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Pearl has said that once the content operation is stable, she wants to support
        advocates working on family-court reform — starting with
        <a href="https://www.redonkulas.com" rel="noopener">Terrence Popp</a> and
        <strong>Second Class Citizen</strong>. No grant amount, schedule, or restricted
        contribution route is represented on this site until the parties confirm it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>What the published terms confirm</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>
        Contributions are voluntary and do not create a right to goods, services, or
        equity unless a separate written agreement says otherwise.
      </li>
      <li>
        Card payments are processed by Stripe; The Audacity Network says it does not
        store payment-card information on its servers.
      </li>
      <li>Its published terms describe contributions as final and non-refundable except where law requires otherwise.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Who is accountable</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p>
      <strong>Pearl Davis</strong> — founder and operator of JustPearlyThings, LLC.
      Directly responsible for how funds are spent within the LLC.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Pearl has publicly discussed forming or operating a nonprofit with Terrence Popp
      involved. This site does not identify that entity as a recipient until its legal
      name, tax status, board, and payment route are confirmed.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reporting standard</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="muted">
      No annual report, audit, Form 990, or event ledger has been supplied for
      publication yet. This page will link primary documents when the responsible
      entity provides them; it will not imply that an audit or filing exists before it does.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Confirmed event totals and allocations can be added to the
      <a href="/events">events page</a> after each fundraiser. No sample totals are
      displayed as real records.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Rails and processors</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul class="clean">
      <li><strong>Card donations</strong> — processed by Stripe on The Audacity Network.</li>
      <li><strong>Cash App</strong> — <code>{DONATION_RAILS.cashApp}</code></li>
      <li><strong>Venmo</strong> — <code>{DONATION_RAILS.venmo}</code></li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cryptocurrency</strong> — addresses are being re-verified against an
        official source and will appear on the donate page only after Pearl personally
        confirms them. Sending crypto to an unverified address is irreversible; the
        engineering standard here is 100% or nothing.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="muted">
      For questions about an existing contribution or the entity shown at checkout,
      write to
      <a href="mailto:production@theaudacitynetwork.com">production@theaudacitynetwork.com</a>
      with the date, amount, and payment method. Do not include a full card number or
      other sensitive financial information.
    </p>
  </div>

  <EmailSignup compact />
</Base>

<style>
  ul.clean { padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0; }
  ul.clean li { margin: 0.35rem 0; }
</style>
